    {
      "type": "h2",
      "text": "Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "1. Why do white spots appear after braces? They form from plaque buildup and mineral loss on the tooth enamel around brackets, usually due to poor oral hygiene or sugary acidic diets. 2. Can white spots on teeth be removed? Yes, treatments like tooth remineralization, whitening and polishing treatments, or dental veneers can reduce or hide white spots after braces effectively. 3. How can I prevent white spots during braces? Practice proper oral hygiene, use fluoride toothpaste, rinse with fluoride mouthwash, and limit sugary and acidic foods daily. 4. Are white spots a sign of tooth decay? They’re early warnings of tooth decay, showing mineral loss in enamel. Treating early helps protect dental health and keeps your oral health stable. 5. Who should treat white spots after braces? A skilled cosmetic dentist can suggest whitening treatments, tooth-colored dental resin, or aesthetic polishing treatment to restore your new smile safely."
    }
